  "claim": "Charles Rousselière has appeared in the the opera written by Charpentier. The opera that it is the sequel to, has more acts than the opera Le roi malgré lui.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Louise (opera). Sentence: Louise is an opera (\"roman musical\" ) in four acts by Gustave Charpentier to an original French libretto by the composer, with some contributions by Saint-Pol-Roux, a symbolist poet and inspiration of the surrealists.\nPage: Le roi malgré lui. Sentence: Le roi malgré lui (\"King in Spite of Himself\" or \"The reluctant king\") is an opéra-comique in three acts by Emmanuel Chabrier of 1887 with an original libretto by Emile de Najac and Paul Burani.\nPage: Julien (opera). Sentence: \"Julien\" is a sequel to Charpentier's \"Louise\" (1900) and describes the artistic aspirations of Louise’s suitor Julien.\nPage: Charles Rousselière. Sentence: He sang in the world premieres of several operas, including the title role in Charpentier's \"Julien\" and Giorgio in Mascagni's \"Amica\"",
  "evidence_text": "Page: Louise (opera). Sentence: Louise is an opera (\"roman musical\" ) in four acts by Gustave Charpentier to an original French libretto by the composer, with some contributions by Saint-Pol-Roux, a symbolist poet and inspiration of the surrealists.\nPage: Le roi malgré lui. Sentence: Le roi malgré lui (\"King in Spite of Himself\" or \"The reluctant king\") is an opéra-comique in three acts by Emmanuel Chabrier of 1887 with an original libretto by Emile de Najac and Paul Burani.\nPage: Julien (opera). Sentence: \"Julien\" is a sequel to Charpentier's \"Louise\" (1900) and describes the artistic aspirations of Louise’s suitor Julien.\nPage: Charles Rousselière. Sentence: He sang in the world premieres of several operas, including the title role in Charpentier's \"Julien\" and Giorgio in Mascagni's \"Amica\"",
